EFI framebuffer reservation on FreeBSD
=====================================

vt(efifb) can keep drawing until drmfb attaches. The firmware framebuffer may
start partway into the GPU's VRAM BAR. Reserving only its length leaves the tail
available to driver allocations, including the GART table.

The MacBookPro16,1 probe reports BAR 0xb0000000, EFI framebuffer 0xb0600000,
length 0x1ea0000. Its end is VRAM offset 0x24a0000; the old reservation ends at
0x1ea0000 and allows a GART table at 0x1f00000 inside the framebuffer.
Initially valid writeback PTEs later read zero and the graphics queue times out.
Additional console logging changes this outcome and is not part of the fix.

The FreeBSD-only patch reserves through the EFI framebuffer's end when metadata
identifies a range wholly within this GPU's BAR. Missing metadata, another GPU,
invalid/overflowing ranges and a larger existing reservation are handled without
shrinking the existing reservation. Linux behavior is unchanged.

After make patch, run on a native FreeBSD worker with Python and a C compiler:
  python3.12 files/test-efifb-reservation.py --source \
    "$(make -V WRKSRC)/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_gmc.c"

The test compiles the actual patched helper and covers the captured overlap,
missing metadata, another GPU, exact BAR bounds, overflowing ranges and retaining
a larger existing reservation. Hardware results must be recorded separately.
